# Compound-target (B/W mixing zone) variant of slag_w.recycle.
# S channels use 3D Y(E,theta,c_B) tables from RustBCA compound targets;
# 'conc B' keys the lookup to the local mixing-zone boron fraction (the
# composition dependence is inside the table -- no linear 'mat' weight).
# T reflection channels keep the pure-pair tables + 'mat' weighting until
# compound reflection tables are ingested (PLAN week 2).
W --> W
T w_on_w mat W
W --> W
A 0.0
W --> W
S w_on_bw_w conc B
W --> B
S w_on_bw_b conc B
W+ --> W
T w_on_w mat W
W+ --> W
A 0.0
W+ --> W
S w_on_bw_w conc B
W+ --> B
S w_on_bw_b conc B
W2+ --> W
T w_on_w mat W
W2+ --> W
A 0.0
W2+ --> W
S w_on_bw_w conc B
W2+ --> B
S w_on_bw_b conc B
W3+ --> W
T w_on_w mat W
W3+ --> W
A 0.0
W3+ --> W
S w_on_bw_w conc B
W3+ --> B
S w_on_bw_b conc B
B --> B
T b_on_b mat B
B --> B
A 0.0
B --> W
S b_on_bw_w conc B
B --> B
S b_on_bw_b conc B
B+ --> B
T b_on_b mat B
B+ --> B
A 0.0
B+ --> W
S b_on_bw_w conc B
B+ --> B
S b_on_bw_b conc B
B2+ --> B
T b_on_b mat B
B2+ --> B
A 0.0
B2+ --> W
S b_on_bw_w conc B
B2+ --> B
S b_on_bw_b conc B
B3+ --> B
T b_on_b mat B
B3+ --> B
A 0.0
B3+ --> W
S b_on_bw_w conc B
B3+ --> B
S b_on_bw_b conc B
B4+ --> B
T b_on_b mat B
B4+ --> B
A 0.0
B4+ --> W
S b_on_bw_w conc B
B4+ --> B
S b_on_bw_b conc B
B5+ --> B
T b_on_b mat B
B5+ --> B
A 0.0
B5+ --> W
S b_on_bw_w conc B
B5+ --> B
S b_on_bw_b conc B
